<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liu Ye</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Queen Soma, Soma of Funan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liu Ye ('Willow Leaf') is the legendary first ruler of Funan, a queen named in Chinese histories from the 3rd century onward. According to them, she led an attack on a foreign ship but was defeated by its passenger Kaundinya, or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaundinya-i">Hun Tian</a>, who married her and founded the ruling line. Later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> tradition identifies her with Soma, a naga princess, as the ancestress of Cambodian kings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liu-ye.jpg" alt="Liu Ye" width="320" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kiensvay · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_of_Kaundinya_I_and_Queen_Soma.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
